{"hash":"5854ae9b30df183c","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":88.044,"said":"Walk slowly along these high walls. See the carvings: elephants, horsemen, hunters, scenes from Shiva’s stories. Let me tell you a story the temple itself loves to tell, from the Srisaila Khanda of the Skanda Purana. Long ago, across the river Krishna, there ruled a king named Chandragupta, and he had a daughter, Chandravati. From childhood her heart belonged to Shiva. In a valley nearby, a waterfall tumbled down carrying countless white jasmine flowers, so many that the pool below looked covered in snow. There she worshipped a linga, and the place came to be called Mallika Theertham, the jasmine pool. With her parents’ blessing she came here to Srisailam to worship. The Chenchu people of these forests loved her like a daughter; they built her a little hut and brought her honey and fruit. Pleased by her devotion, Shiva offered her a boon. She asked for only one thing: that he should always wear the jasmine garland she made for him. And so, the story says, he became Mallikarjuna, the lord adorned with mallika, the jasmine. But there is another story behind that name, a story of a mother, a father and a son. Come into the court.\n\nDid you know? Mallika Theertham, the jasmine pool of the story, is a real waterfall-fed pool about 54 km from Srisailam.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1144},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1160,"end":1266}],"words":[[0.098,0.252,0,4],[0.362,0.481,5,11],[0.855,0.361,12,17],[1.228,0.24,18,23],[1.48,0.216,24,28],[1.709,0.517,29,34],[3.149,0.228,36,39],[3.389,0.12,40,43],[3.522,0.601,44,52],[4.315,0.637,54,63],[5.084,0.637,65,73],[5.913,0.661,75,82],[6.791,0.385,84,90],[7.188,0.228,91,95],[7.428,0.505,96,103],[7.945,0.601,104,111],[9.447,0.264,113,116],[9.724,0.12,117,119],[9.856,0.252,120,124],[10.12,0.18,125,128],[10.312,0.072,129,130],[10.397,0.469,131,136],[10.877,0.12,137,140],[11.01,0.409,141,147],[11.43,0.457,148,154],[11.899,0.3,